  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Accenture Federal Services recorded $3.2B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date, with 434 awards and an average award size of $7.4M. Obligations fell 0.5% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations have risen from $2.5B in FY21 to $3.2B in FY25, and FY26 is reported at $3.2B so far. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer this year with $559M in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy with $455M and the Department of Education with $372M. Computer Systems Design Services is the dominant market with $2.8B in obligations. Other notable markets include Other Computer Related Services at $183M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $96.8M. The dataset shows concentrated demand in IT services and related professional services, and a broad agency footprint that includes civilian and defense customers. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing, and the page notes award-value figures in some tables represent total contract values rather than obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Accenture Federal Services obligations rose from $2.5B in FY21 to $3.4B in FY24, then were $3.2B in FY25 and $3.2B in FY26 to date. Obligations fell 0.5% year over year for the current reporting period. The average award size in FY2026 to date is $7.4M across 434 awards."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and what markets drive revenue?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer at $559M, followed by the Department of Energy at $455M and the Department of Education at $372M. Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market at $2.8B, with Other Computer Related Services at $183M and Custom Computer Programming Services at $96.8M also contributing."
      }
    ]
  },
